  ],
  reason: "A required floor that never Strict-prepares an untouched module cannot typecheck it, so a declaration whose INTERFACE changes in another module strands its readers silently: a coproduct growing an arm under an exhaustive match (gunbc#11194), a product field retyped and an alias re-branded under an untouched witness (gunbc#11751, found by #12077, repaired by #12120; gunbc.recurring_failure_mode changed_declaration_signature_consumer_unplanned). Two halves: seed the touched module (dependency direction, gunbc#11252) and seed the untouched READERS of every declaration whose interface differs between the floor's own resolved diff base and head (dependents direction). The readers are derived from the consumption relation declaring_candidates over the parse phase's DeclarationIndex -- never every importer -- and are ground-specific: pure arm growth plans match readers only; a changed signature, a removed declaration, an arm set that lost an arm or changed a payload or its residual interface, and a change propagated through another declaration's INTERFACE (resolved or flat-channel) plan every reader; a caller roster introduced plans every reader it does not admit, a roster narrowed plans only the dropped callers, and a roster widened or removed plans nobody. The interface is read from ModuleDeclarationRecord fields the parse phase already fills (declaration interface text, interface type references, caller rosters, per-arm texts, coproduct residuals, declaration-grain call and value occurrences, both with in-scope lexical shadowing applied by one containment authority) -- no second relation -- and the planned readers are prepared through the SAME closure path. THE SEAM, STATED HONESTLY: v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed is the modeled authority for the grounds, the read dispositions, the reader populations and the propagation rule; this Rust is an enumerated bootstrap MIRROR of those decisions -- it classifies grounds, propagates and selects -- not merely a realization of the index, and the two are kept in agreement by the paired claims on each side. reconstruct_base_index is the base-side reconstruction the deleted wave-admission wall shared (gunbc.rung_drop namespace_wave_admission_wall_removed); module_name_is_or_is_contained_by is the segment-bounded rule for module-name seeds. Out-of-root touched files and readers are typed rows, not counts. THE MODULE KEEPS ITS arm_set NAME deliberately: it is this hand-Rust's v1-freeze admission record, cited by gunbc.seed_growth_admission and gunbc.namespace_baseline_seed_growth, and its identity is the admission history (gunbc#11194 first admitted it); renaming it would rewrite that citation surface to change a label while the admitted items -- every one enumerated above -- are what the record is about.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "The selector, its records and the planning enum follow gunbc.declaration_index_seed_growth's first step: the moment the per-module declaration record is a .dag carrier, interface_changed_consumers is an ordinary fold over it beside declaring_candidates and moves with them, and v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed consumes it directly instead of being mirrored. reconstruct_base_index follows the scm lane with git_stdout and base_records: when a typed repository-read transport can supply a file's text at a ref. The seed-list plumbing in run_required_floor and module_name_is_or_is_contained_by dissolve when preparation is a modeled operation over PreparedSubjectSeedGround rather than two string lists. The tests are the evidence and retire only as regression controls when the wall climbs; a fixture that greens when the invocation lands flips to a permanent control, it does not retire.",
  current_boundary: "Reachable only from the required floor's planning row (run_required_floor, witnesses lane); the wall's own runner is deleted with the wall (operator ruling 2026-09-19). Decides nothing for gunbc compile, claim_batch or any per-entry path. Widens the prepared subject by exactly the touched modules and the ground-specific READERS of declarations whose interface changed -- match readers for pure arm growth, every resolved or flat-channel reader for a signature change, removal, breaking arm-set change or interface propagation, the non-admitted readers for an introduced caller roster, the dropped callers for a narrowed one, nobody for a widened or removed roster or a body-only edit -- each announced with its ground on the run's own receipt line, and narrows nothing: a base that cannot be reconstructed on a CI commit REFUSES the floor rather than planning blind, and a local run without a diff baseline reports the projection unevaluated exactly as the changed-witness projection already does. BOUND: a reader outside the floor roots is planned and counted, not prepared; an unresolved name occurrence plans nothing; a reader reaching the declaration only through an inferred type no declaration on the path spells is not reached; a formatting-only signature edit over-plans its readers.",
}
